  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal, written-style verb. In everyday conversation, {減|へ}らす (transitive) or {減|へ}る (intransitive) are far more common. {減|げん}じる appears in legal, administrative, and academic writing.\n\nThe variant {減|げん}ずる (classical conjugation) is also used and carries an even more formal tone.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {刑|けい}を{減|げん}じる: to reduce a sentence\n- {税|ぜい}を{減|げん}じる: to reduce taxes\n- {経費|けいひ}を{減|げん}じる: to reduce expenses\n- {負担|ふたん}を{減|げん}じる: to reduce a burden\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {減|へ}らす: to reduce (everyday transitive)\n- {減|へ}る: to decrease (everyday intransitive)\n- {減少|げんしょう}する: to decrease (formal, noun + suru)",
